Local Computer

Your code: boomRebecca
You make changes to files here
2. Git Commit (Local)

git add → stages your changes
git commit → saves changes to local git history
Still only on your computer at this point
3. GitHub Push

git push origin main → uploads to GitHub
Repository: https://github.com/daymaker2day-rgb/beccaboom
Now visible on GitHub website
4. GitHub Pages (Automatic)

GitHub detects the push to main branch
Automatically builds the site (runs build process)
Takes 1-5 minutes to complete
Publishes to GitHub Pages server
5. Live Website

Final destination: https://daymaker2day-rgb.github.io/beccaboom/
Anyone can access it here
Your daughter logs in with password here
Summary Flow:


Your PC → Git Commit → Git Push → GitHub Repo → GitHub Pages Build → Live Site(local)     (local)      (upload)   (stored)      (auto-builds)      (public)
That's why there's a delay - step 4 (GitHub Pages building) takes a few minutes after you push!